{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array of content type "},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first, each with two members: "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, and "},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds it; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and no other device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its unique users are sessions. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, rather than an event with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Mixpanel would attribute to no user,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events of the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as one, so a recovered record that Mixpanel had already stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The record’s vendor identifier and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name and version","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" Mixpanel takes, and one too large for Mixpanel ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. Mixpanel answers a request it reads with 200, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" retries one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"413. Mixpanel answers 200 as well when it ingests none of a request’s events: a wrong region,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored, so check the project’s Live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"View after setting it up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days: a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"older than that when it is sent, such as one a store kept through a long time offline, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted as delivered and not stored. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"text":". The bytes are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L83","fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"